※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4372
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4372 LANG_RELRO_HOLDS_WHAT_CHANGES

※ A `@[relro]` variable holds nothing that can change without the variable
※ being written.  A dictionary whose entries may change is changed through its
※ type and not through the variable -- an entry put in asks the table, not the
※ name -- and a field written `mut` through its own mark; neither asks whether
※ the variable may be written, so a change after the startup function would be
※ refused by nothing and would write what the entry point had made read-only.

let std := ⎕import("std")

type Counter = mut n : u32

@[relro]
let names: mut ⸨str: u8⸩ = ⸨"a": 1u8⸩

@[relro]
let counted: mut Counter = Counter(.n ← 0u32)

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    ⎕narrow(#names + counted.n, ⌜u6⌝) ?? 0u6
